      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "BLOOM's operational model is characterized by lean, volunteer-led management that maximizes the impact of every donation. In FY2023, the organization reported <cite id=\"10\">total revenue of $158,297</cite> while keeping administrative costs remarkably low. Their impact is tangible and well-documented; for instance, they have successfully <cite id=\"11\">built 11 PlayGardens</cite> and provided <cite id=\"12\">700,000 meals in Gaza</cite> as of their latest reports. This ability to pivot from infrastructure projects to emergency food relief demonstrates high organizational agility. Furthermore, the charity maintains <cite id=\"13\">21.3 months of working capital</cite>, providing a massive buffer for financial stability and long-term project sustainability."
      ],
      "summary": "BLOOM Charity is a specialized humanitarian organization dedicated to the mental health and physical well-being of vulnerable children, particularly orphans and those in crisis zones. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">2015</cite>, the charity has developed a unique niche by providing <cite id=\"2\">therapeutic PlayGardens and childhood enrichment</cite> alongside emergency relief. In FY2024, the organization demonstrated significant growth, with <cite id=\"3\">revenue reaching $551,810</cite>, up from $158,297 in FY2023. Despite this rapid expansion, BLOOM has maintained an <cite id=\"4\">exceptional program expense ratio of 98.7%</cite> according to its latest filings, ensuring that donor funds are directed almost entirely to frontline services. The organization's work spans critical regions including <cite id=\"5\">Morocco, Palestine, and Pakistan</cite>, where it addresses the psychological toll of displacement and poverty. By focusing on the 'right to play,' BLOOM fills a vital gap in traditional humanitarian aid, which often overlooks the developmental and emotional needs of children in favor of purely physical survival. Their operations are <cite id=\"6\">verified as zakat-eligible</cite>, serving the poor (fuqara) and needy (masakin) through direct aid and infrastructure projects.",
